{{!
    A stock transfer is a document, same shape as the two order documents — SCREENS.md
    section F: "Detail is a document view".

    Buttons go in Layout::Section::Header's block; the component has no @actionButtons
    argument, so passing one renders nothing.

    Two more things about that component, both found by measuring rather than reading:

    1. The status pill is @badge, NOT @status. All three documents passed @status, which
       the component ignores, so none of them had ever shown a status pill.
    2. No @subtitle. The subheader is `grid-template-columns: 1fr 3fr`, so the title
       column is a fixed quarter of the width whatever it contains — 243px here. A
       destination warehouse name wrapped the transfer number onto two lines inside it
       while three quarters of the header sat empty. The same fact is one panel below
       under ROUTE.
}}
<Layout::Container>
    <Layout::Section>
        <Layout::Section::Header @title={{@model.transfer_number}} @badge={{@model.status}}>
            {{#each this.actionButtons as |button|}}
                <Button @icon={{button.icon}} @type={{or button.type "default"}} @text={{button.text}} @onClick={{button.fn}} @wrapperClass="ml-2" />
            {{/each}}
            <Button @icon="list" @type="default" @text={{t "operations.transfers.back-to-list"}} @onClick={{transition-to "operations.transfers.index"}} @wrapperClass="ml-2" />
        </Layout::Section::Header>

        <Layout::Section::Body>
            <div class="space-y-3 p-4">
                {{outlet}}
            </div>
        </Layout::Section::Body>
    </Layout::Section>
</Layout::Container>
